          "evaluated": true,
          "expectation_delta": "Onsemi expects AI-data-center revenue to rise from more than $500 million in 2026 to at least $2.5 billion by 2030 and projects server-rack power consumption to rise from roughly 100–120 kW to megawatt scale. This increases confidence in the scale and persistence of physical AI power demand and the addressable need for onsite firm power, although it does not assign share or orders to Bloom.",
          "prior_expectation": "AI-data-center demand was already a BE growth driver, but the pre-event baseline lacked a new independent supplier forecast quantifying both the rise in rack-level power intensity and the associated value of power components. BE still required customer deployments and accepted MW to convert that market into revenue.",
